When a person repeats an action, the brain strengthens the neural pathways connected to it, turning that action into a habit. Over time, the brain starts to crave that dopamine release, making the habit harder to break. This is also why it's so important to build healthy habits early on, because our brains are still growing and learning how to manage impulse control! 

